---
import Resumen from "../../layouts/Resumen.astro";

/**
 * The address cannot be an address.
 *
 * **The one refusal on this path that is about the submitted field and is still safe to
 * speak**, and the distinction is worth being exact about, because the identical-response
 * rule looks like it forbids this page.
 *
 * It does not. That rule closes an *enumeration oracle*: the form must not answer whether an
 * address belongs to a subscriber. This page answers something else entirely — that what was
 * typed is not shaped like an email at all — and it says nothing whatsoever about
 * `perez@gmail.com` when the form was given `perez@gmial`. The sign-in form takes the
 * opposite line and refuses to speak at all, because there the address either belongs to a
 * shelter or belongs to nobody, and "no such address" *is* the enumeration answer.
 *
 * What speaking buys is the case silence handles worst: an adopter with a typo who would
 * otherwise wait three days for a mail that was never going anywhere.
 */
---

<Resumen title="Revisa el correo" heading="Ese correo no se puede usar">
  <p data-testid="bad-address">
    Como está escrito no es una dirección de correo, así que no hay dónde mandarte el resumen.
    Revísalo y vuelve a intentar.
  </p>

  <p>
    <!--
      Said plainly, because the page above it is the one that cannot say it. A subscriber who
      has just been told "we cannot use that address" should not be left wondering whether we
      looked it up.
    -->
    No buscamos el correo en ninguna parte: lo único que vimos es que le falta algo para ser
    una dirección.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/resumen">Volver al formulario</a></p>
</Resumen>
